<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Cures</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Cures Sabini</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Cures was an ancient town of the Sabines north-east of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a>, near modern Fara in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sabina">Sabina</a>. Roman legend made it the home of the Sabine king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/titus-tatius">Titus Tatius</a> and of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/numa-pompilius">Numa Pompilius</a>, Rome's second king. Ancient writers derived Quirites, a name for the citizens of Rome, from Cures.</p></div>
